# The installer ships these files exactly as they sit on disk, so a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true (the GitHub runner default) used to ship CRLF
# text files and the installed copies stopped matching the repository. Pin LF for
# the whole tree; git still treats binaries as binary. npm run check fails when a
# shipped file comes out CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Keep the prompt comparison EOL-proof: the sync test compares against
# STT_SYSTEM_PROMPT (\n), so this file always checks out with LF even when
# core.autocrlf is true on Windows.
prompts/stt-system-prompt.md text eol=lf
